[Music]  everyone has heard the stories about  what happened back in 68 the most brutal  series of occult murders in wyoming  history  ten victims killed over a series of four  months found with their hearts cut out  near some old cabin out in the sticks  all these innocent people's lives were  cut short in the service of worshiping  some entity that nobody else understood  thankfully the murders had stopped by  the start of the 70s and this humble  wyoming county knew nothing but peace  for several years after but the cabin  where it all happened remained abandoned  the ground was sour there weighed down  by the horrors that transpired you need  to be brave or foolish to set foot there  all things considered that's what led 17  year old charlie and his reluctant  girlfriend samantha to that rickety old  building one cold dark winter night he  was doing what most foolhardy teenage  boys tried to do with almost every  action they took  prove himself  samantha was just along for the ride  despite her protests her folks had  always warned her about this place the  word they most often used to describe it  was  evil  but charlie wouldn't take no for an  answer he was going to open that rickety  front door and step inside and samantha  would watch in awe of his bravery though  as he got closer and felt his fingers  nearing the door handle a pang of fear  tingled through him was this really  something he wanted to do too late to  back out now  samantha was watching he couldn't be a  coward he needed to commit he needed to  prove he could do this charlie took a  final deep breath  opened the door and stepped through into  the dark he would never be seen again  samantha squinted and looked into the  dark there was no into really it was  like a giant black rectangle was  obscuring the doorway there was no way  to make out any of the features inside  she called her boyfriend's name with a  quivering voice and got nothing in  response that's when she should have  started running it might have even saved  her a figure emerged from the door  walking fast it was solid black with no  discernible features only a vaguely  humanoid shape it walked towards her  with such speed and purpose that poor  samantha didn't even have time to scream  the creature extended a clawed hand and  reached through her chest it didn't even  break the skin  just face through her skin muscle and  bone like a ghost passing through a wall  suddenly she felt immense pain as the  creature drew back its hand it was  holding something that moved and  squirmed in its clawed grip it was only  as samantha collapsed her vision going  dark for the last time that she realized  she was looking at her own beating heart  and this wouldn't be where the horrors  ended for this little wyoming town  now this was only the beginning  more people would go missing in the  following days and weeks wildlife and  livestock would also be found dead under  mysterious circumstances local vets were  baffled by dead pets found in yards with  no obvious cause of death only to be  confused and horrified when they  performed an autopsy and found massive  internal bleeding and a missing heart  despite the fact that there was never  any kind of wound indicating a heart's  removal your average weird occult  murders are the fbi's problem but when  hearts start to disappear in a  mysterious fashion that's how the scp  foundation gets involved in your case  they dispatched a number of field agents  into the town in order to track down the  source of this anomalous activity and  potentially secure and contain whatever  hostile entity was behind it in this  case they really didn't need to track  the entity down  it came for them  three agents were driving down a lonely  wyoming road near the cabin when a  sudden series of shapes glowed into  prominence in the car's high beams it  wasn't just one of those vantablack  creatures  it was several the second the car ground  to a halt the entities engaged with  extreme hostility they attacked  seemingly unaffected by conventional  arms fire from the two agents in the  front seats they dragged them out of the  car before reaching into their chests  and pulling out their hearts the agent  in the back seat got lucky he'd had  experience with being similar to this in  the past and had one method that might  work as they drew towards him he loaded  a magazine of silver-tipped rounds into  his handgun closer closer the agent also  happened to be a devout muslim and as  the creatures approached he drew his  weapon and prayed to allah for the  strength to overcome these demons he  opened fire just as they were climbing  into the car and reaching for him for  the first time the bullets seemed to  have an effect the creatures squealed as  the gunfire rendered through them the  one stealth fatal wounds briefly  convulsed before melting into a fine  sulphuric sludge the agent thinking on  his feet noticed that the creatures that  stole the hearts of his two fellow  agents were fleeing he followed them  trying to find their source  and of course it was the cabin the  creatures passed back through the open  door into the darkness of the cabin how  many of them were there and what was  going on inside naturally the full mind  of the scp foundation rolled into town  not long after this incident knowing now  that the cabin designated  scp-1983-1 was the source of the  creatures designated scp-1983-2  things were easier to get under control  a fake chemical plant was built around  the cabin as the pretense to keep it  contained this plant became known as  outpost 54. on-site researchers would  sleep in the facility soldiers required  for the regular culling of 1983-2  instances would make their home in the  barracks and of course there was also a  large armory filled with the specialized  weaponry and ammunition required to put  the rampaging heart stealing creatures  down  the fateful encounter that the surviving  agent had with these aggressive entities  provided the foundation with an  invaluable piece of data on how to  combat scp-1983  for reasons not fully understood the  1983-2 creatures have an extreme  reaction against sincere human belief it  doesn't matter which religion you  personally follow if you are a true  believer and you make a prayer to your  deity of choice while firing on one of  these monsters with silver-based  ammunition you will be able to slay them  brings a whole new meaning to the phrase  spray and pray  but the belief must be truly sincere for  the attack to work if there is doubt or  skepticism in your heart when you're  praying and firing well let's just say  it won't be your heart for much longer  these very particular killing methods  are the reason that mtf kai 13 also  known as the choir boys were brought in  to be the personal stewards of 1983's  containment they're a mobile task force  formed entirely of devout religious  believers whose faith guards them  against the influence of a number of  occult monsters  scp-1983 included the foundation  performed a series of cursory tests on  the cabin itself the building contained  several frustrating spatial anomalies  with the locus of these being the front  door and the living room behind it the  living room seemed impossible to access  by any means other than the anomalous  aperture in the front door any attempts  to enter it via the wall or other doors  in the house simply caused the  researchers to pop up in different areas  of the house  after a barrage of tests including  busting holes in the exterior walls in  an attempt to enter two no avail of  course the o5 council forbade further  testing it simply wasn't worth  potentially creating more openings that  1983-2 instances could emerge from  this left only one option  launching excursions into the heart of  the anomaly itself via the portal in the  front door  this seemed to be the only way to  successfully gather intel about the  inner workings for the first of three  fateful incidents a detachment from the  choir boys armed with silver munitions  were sent into the portal none of them  ever returned but for the first time in  years the front door mysteriously closed  again this led to a drastic reduction in  the release of scp-1983-2  instances but still left a whole team  potentially stranded inside a second  detachment from the choir boys was  prepared to head in and if not rescue at  least find out what happened to the  first they opened the door and ventured  inside only for history to repeat itself  not one of them would ever be seen alive  again  and what's more with the door once again  open another one of the entities soon  charged out and began attacking more  foundation researchers the onslaught  stopped only with the brave sacrifice of  agent morris a field agent stationed at  outpost 54 at the time he entered the  doorway and closed the door once again  from the inside just like everyone else  agent morris was sadly never seen alive  again but on may 23 1989  something remarkable happened having  wasted too many agents on this anomaly  already the foundation decided to send  in a d-class the d-class in question was  jackson parker a man whose personnel  file indicated that he had a profound  belief in the moral fairness of the  universe that everything that happened  simply must have happened for a reason  even his own incarceration he was given  a camera with a live feed and a lifeline  leading back outside before practically  being pushed into the cabin moments  later the lifeline was pulled taut and  snapped the feed cut off at around the  same time foundation researchers at the  outpost side having lost another guinea  pig little did they know jackson parker  wasn't dead and what's more he was about  to do what no agent of the scp  foundation could destroy scp-1983  on the inside jackson was met with a  nightmare this anomaly was so much worse  than anyone knew it didn't look like the  inside of a cabin it was a surreal  shadow dimension looking like a  patchwork amalgamation of so many  different buildings  hospitals schools offices homes  factories military installations  jackson even recognized the dingy  basement of his childhood home among the  chaos at that moment it was clear  this wasn't just one anomalous location  it was the nexus point for many how many  doors were there out there in how many  different buildings unleashing the  horrors of  scp-1983 across the world  across dimensions even lucky for jackson  he was about to receive a little help  from beyond the grave one of the choir  boys agent barclay had written a note  before he died here he gave the few  pieces of information jackson needed not  only to survive but potentially even  destroy this thing once and for all  first that the entities born from the  shadows are weaker in the dark light  gives them form in the dark they're  intangible second there is no way out  through the front door if someone tries  to escape outside their body will melt  almost instantaneously  and most importantly of all agent  barkley realized why they'd been taking  the hearts in the center of this  terrible place lies the nest a giant  pile of human hearts surrounded by light  sources acting as a kind of incubator  after being placed in the nest the  hearts burst open and new instances of  scp-1983-2 emerge if someone could  destroy the nest it may destroy the very  heart of scp-1983  and finally neutralized this nightmarish  anomaly agent barkley had lost his faith  seeing his friends slaughtered around  him so he didn't have it in himself to  finish this thing it could only be  jackson now and as you know jackson had  an unshakable belief that everything  happens for a reason perhaps the reason  he was here was to finally bring an end  to the suffering and that's exactly what  he was going to do  jackson shouldered barclay's rifle and  charged through the labyrinth gunning  down attacking scp-1983-2  entities on the way he was a man on a  mission soon he made his way into the  central chamber and finally saw it the  nest this horrifying pile of wriggling  human hearts one of the many sights that  finally broke agent barclay but jackson  stood unbroken he aimed the rifle at the  nest and opened fire the sheer force of  his unshakable belief supercharging his  every shot he had struck a killing blow  at the heart of the beast avenging  everyone it had ever murdered on the  outside to everyone's amazement  scp-1983 disappeared the front door  opened and the darkness dissipated  within when agents and researchers  entered they found the desiccated corpse  of several mobile task force members but  all signs of the previous anomaly were  gone from the same note left on the  corpse of agent barclay it was clear to  researchers that jackson parker had  taken the advice  and finally neutralized this dangerous  ketter class anomaly though jackson  himself was nowhere to be found he was  given a posthumous medal of bravery and  merit by the foundation only one of two  ever awarded to a d-class  i guess you could say that everything  happens for a reason now go check out  scp-3999 i'm at the center of everything  that happens to me at scp-5049 the skin  salesman demon dan's discount homunculus  depot for more explorations into the  hearts of genuinely unnerving scps

